        "content_ANFq87": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A Bespoke Specification",
            "title_size": "xl",
            "text": "Rather than applying a standard scheme throughout the building, the specification included a considerable amount of variation between different rooms and areas - bedrooms formed a major part of this, with fitted and freestanding pieces supplied across the home. <br> <br>\nOne of the more distinctive elements was the bespoke fitted bedroom furniture, including substantial 2.1m-high triple wardrobes in a cashmere finish. The scale of these pieces gave the bedrooms a strong, built-in appearance while also providing the perfect amount of storage required within each room.\nUnlike a straightforward freestanding furniture order, fitted elements also required closer coordination with the dimensions and layout of the building. Manufacturing tolerances and site measurements needed to align before installation could be completed.",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_action": "link",
            "button_url": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "images_wVPABn",
        "content_ANFq87"
      ],
      "name": "Image - Text",
      "settings": {
        "colour_scheme": "base-white-01",
        "section_padding": "--spacing-2xl",
        "contact_form_html": "",
        "enable_reveal": true,
        "reveal_distance": 32,
        "reveal_duration": 760
      }
    },
    "image_text_nRYrfd": {
      "type": "image-text",
      "blocks": {
        "content_6rxGTr": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The Finer Details",
            "title_size": "xl",
            "text": "The bedroom furniture was only one part of the bespoke specification, as across Willow Lodge, a number of pieces required additional development to achieve the details set out within the interior scheme. Among the 130 windows across the home we dressed with bespoke curtains and blinds, a distinctive example was those in the café, where curved pelmets were produced. Rather than using a standard straight pelmet, the curved design highlighted the architecture and character of the interior, requiring a more bespoke approach to manufacture and installation.",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_action": "link",
            "button_url": ""
          }
        },
        "images_gHUjBg": {
          "type": "images",
          "settings": {
            "image_one": "shopify://shop_images/Cafe_with_blinds.png"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "content_6rxGTr",
        "images_gHUjBg"
      ],
      "name": "Image - Text",
      "settings": {
        "colour_scheme": "base-white-01",
        "section_padding": "--spacing-2xl",
        "contact_form_html": "",
        "enable_reveal": true,
        "reveal_distance": 32,
        "reveal_duration": 760
      }
    },
    "image_text_P8d8bJ": {
      "type": "image-text",
      "blocks": {
        "images_NqCAd6": {
          "type": "images",
          "settings": {
            "image_one": "shopify://shop_images/Willow_Lodge_Vol_2-14_46ea5ce0-e03a-4a46-8f0d-0da9593db8cb.jpg"
          }
        },
        "content_ENmpa7": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Delivering At Scale",
            "title_size": "xl",
            "text": "With more than 2,300 individual items to bring to site, delivery and installation was a significant part of the project. More than 30 van loads were coordinated over the course of the fit-out, resulting in over 725 driver hours on site. <br> <br>\n\nInstallation took place while work was still progressing across the building, with decorating underway in some areas and external groundworks still at an early stage. As different rooms became available at different times, deliveries had to be carefully coordinated around the progress on site. <br> <br>\n\nOur white-glove delivery service meant the process continued further than just getting furniture to the door - our drivers took items directly to their intended rooms, where they assembled the furniture and positioned it ready for use. Across a project of this scale, this approach ensured the smoothest install for the home.",
            "button_style": "underline",
            "button_text": "Our Delivery Service",
            "button_action": "link",
            "button_url": "shopify://pages/delivery"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "images_NqCAd6",
        "content_ENmpa7"
      ],
      "name": "Image - Text",
      "settings": {
        "colour_scheme": "base-white-01",
        "section_padding": "--spacing-2xl",
        "contact_form_html": "",
        "enable_reveal": true,
        "reveal_distance": 32,
        "reveal_duration": 760
      }
    },
    "image_text_FgCCAX": {
      "type": "image-text",
      "blocks": {
        "images_bkFGjK": {
          "type": "images",
          "settings": {
            "image_one": "shopify://shop_images/Willow_Lodge_Vol_4-38.jpg"
          }
        },
        "content_ckY3Hk": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Seamless Execution",
            "title_size": "display",
            "text": "From early planning through to final styling, our aim at Manor Park was to create a dementia-friendly environment that felt warm, calm and intuitive to navigate, without ever appearing clinical. Ahead of installation, we supported the client with site visits to previously completed projects alongside a full sampling process, helping shape a consistent look and feel across the 80-bedroom home — from communal areas through to staff offices. Working within a live newbuild meant close coordination with other trades throughout the installation. During installation, a Project Manager and Deputy Project Manager were on site throughout, overseeing a white glove fit-out that saw 5,500 items placed across the home in just 10 days, with zero damages. Our delivery team averaged 17,000 steps per person per day, placing each piece exactly where it was needed. \n<br>\n Beyond furniture supply, we completed the final layers too — installing curtains, artwork and accessories — transforming Manor Park from a blank canvas into a fully functioning, welcoming home ready to receive residents from day one.",
            "button_style": "underline",
            "button_text": "Our Delivery Service",
            "button_action": "link",
            "button_url": "shopify://pages/delivery"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "images_bkFGjK",
        "content_ckY3Hk"
